    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58556" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολάπ-τω</span></b> , of birds, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>peck</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολάψασα ἐξέλεψεν
				τὸν νεοσσόν</span>, of a hen, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Nat.Puer.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τὰ ἕλκη, τὰ
			ὄμματα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				609a35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				b6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἧπαρ</span>, of the eagle
			and Prometheus, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				6
			</span></i> codd.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>, of a crane, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.369
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i> Antec.): metaph., of a man, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠὰ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxil.
					18.4
				</span></i>
			; of rain-drops breaking up the soil, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				30.2
			</span></i>; of horses, <i>strike</i> with the hoof, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Pun.</u>
				129
			</span></i>; of Pegasos, <i>produce by striking</i> the ground with
			his hoof, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρήνην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					15.25.19
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Besant.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>carve, engrave</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμμα εἰς
